# Database

- SQL Server 2022 is the system of record. Liquibase, under `/database`, is the sole source of truth for schema.
- Never create EF Core migrations. Never modify the database schema from application startup. Map a table in EF Core only after its changeset exists.
- Keys are `uniqueidentifier`. Instants are `datetime2` in UTC. Concurrency uses `rowversion`.
- Soft delete with `DeletedAt`. Audit columns are mandatory on business tables.
- Names: PascalCase tables and columns, `PK_TableName`, `FK_Table_ReferencedTable`, `IX_Table_Column`, `usp_Name`, `vw_Name`, `fn_Name`.
- Every changeset has a ticket id, author, rollback, index review, and performance note.
- The master changelog is `database/changelog/db.changelog-master.yaml`. The standard is `docs/Database-Standards.md`.
- Index review order: primary key, foreign keys, unique indexes, composite indexes, filtered indexes, then the reason each index exists.
- Do not add an index that has no query or constraint. Part 1 creates no business tables and no indexes.

```xml
<changeSet id="LF-0001" author="lifefit-architecture">
  <comment>Ticket: LF-0001. Index review: none. Performance note: metadata only.</comment>
  <rollback />
</changeSet>
```
